#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""waifu: every Claude Code window gets its own anime girl and its own background colour.

Official HoYoverse art (Genshin Impact, Honkai: Star Rail, Zenless Zone Zero; wide
wallpapers with the girls, never any males) becomes the Windows Terminal background,
drawn as faint braille dots so your text stays readable. Open windows never change.

  waifu setup [--pool DIR]  one-time install: profiles, shortcut, first wallpapers
  waifu              give this window a different girl
  waifu info         who's in this window (characters, game, where HoYoverse posted it)
  waifu keep         keep this girl forever (cleanup never touches her)
  waifu ban          never show this girl again, and swap her out here
  waifu fetch [N]    download N more wallpapers (default 12)
  waifu style S      dots (default) or image (the full-colour picture)
  waifu opacity PCT  how strong the current style is behind your text
  waifu show FILE [PCT]  pin any image from the wallpaper folder in this window
  waifu off | on     hide them all (screen sharing) / bring them back
  waifu launch       open a new Claude Waifu window from inside WSL
  waifu open         open the wallpaper folder in Explorer
  waifu uninstall    remove the profiles, shortcut and launcher (wallpapers are kept)

How the per-window part works: Windows Terminal draws the background per profile. Setup
adds ten hidden profiles ("slots"). The Claude Waifu shortcut opens a new window on the
slot that already holds the next girl and colour, starts Claude in it, and runs
`waifu advance` to load the slot after that for the next window.

Drop your own .png/.jpg wallpapers into the wallpaper folder and they join the rotation.
"""
